This licence covers the source code and everything written for it, with one
deliberate exception, stated here because a file that carries two licences and
does not say so is worse than one that carries none:

    art/ is NOT covered by the MIT licence above.

The artwork under `art/` is licensed under the Piapro Character Licence (PCL)
where it depicts a Piapro character, and `art/LICENSE` states which files and
under what terms. PCL cannot be sublicensed (第3条第4項), so it cannot be folded
into an MIT grant; PCL 第4条第2項 is what makes the split possible, because it
applies only to the embedded element and not to the work containing it.

See `docs/licensing.md` for the whole situation, with every clause quoted.
